# PRODUCTION — non-secret RUNTIME config (read from process.env by the server).
# Was fly.production.toml [env]. See config/env/README.md and D-70. Genuine
# secrets (Stripe live keys, LIVEKIT_API_SECRET, etc.) stay in Infisical.
#
# NODE_ENV / PORT are set by the Dockerfile (not here).
#
# Differences from preview, all deliberate:
#   - NO Supabase vars: storage is unconditionally R2 in production.
#   - The gated video flags (LESSON_INSIGHTS_TRANSCRIPTION / LIVE_CAPTIONS /
#     CLASS_RECORDING) were off at first; see the block below for which are on
#     today and why (D-16, D-185). The per-student D-22
#     insights-consent check in lib/lesson-notes/consent.ts is independent of
#     these flags and is what gates who actually gets voice captured.

# Server-side Sentry/PostHog — SHARED with preview (same as NEXT_PUBLIC twins).
SENTRY_DSN=__LOCAL__
POSTHOG_KEY=__LOCAL__
POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# Production URLs.
APP_URL=https://spiralclass.com
BETTER_AUTH_URL=https://spiralclass.com

# Production email sender. Requires updates.spiralclass.com SPF/DKIM verified
# in Resend (preview uses the updates.staging.spiralclass.com subdomain).
# D-138: moved 2026-08-29, after updates.spiralclass.com verified in Resend
# (us-east-1, `send` return-path, its own DKIM key — the key copied from the old
# zone was that domain's and was replaced). This address delivers the sign-in
# OTP, so it was held on the old domain until Resend actually said Verified.
RESEND_FROM=soporte@updates.spiralclass.com

# Google Sign-In client — SAME client as preview. The paired
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET is in Infisical. REQUIRED:
# https://spiralclass.com/api/auth/callback/google must be an Authorized
# redirect URI on this client in Google Cloud Console, or Sign-In 400s.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=__LOCAL__

# lib/csp.ts: enforce mode on in production.
CSP_ENFORCE=1

# Intro-video AI coach — deliberately NOT under the D-22 legal
# gate (teacher's OWN public intro video, no student data/minors), so it ships
# enabled. Still a no-op until DEEPGRAM_API_KEY (Infisical) + the teacher-videos
# R2 bucket are set on the production app.
INTRO_VIDEO_COACH_ENABLED=1

# AI-generated social-preview images (D-125) — also NOT under the D-22
# legal gate: a teacher's own marketing image for a share link, no student
# data involved. The upload half of social previews works with this flag off
# (D-125's default is upload-only); this flag turns on the Gemini-generated
# rail specifically. It also needs a Vertex credential — socialPreviewAiEnabled()
# requires both (env.ts). On Cloud Run that credential is the service's own
# runtime identity (web-runtime, holding roles/aiplatform.user), so no secret is
# needed; GEMINI_VERTEX_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY_BASE64 is the off-GCP path and wins
# while it is still set (D-125, 2026-09-24).
SOCIAL_PREVIEW_AI_ENABLED=1

# Vertex AI project the Gemini image-generation call runs against (D-125) —
# NOT a secret, same posture as GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID. Shared with preview: it's
# a GCP project id, not an environment-scoped credential.
GEMINI_VERTEX_PROJECT_ID=__LOCAL__

# Stripe subscription Price IDs (UK entity, D-143). Non-secret identifiers; the
# paired STRIPE_SECRET_KEY / STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET / STRIPE_BILLING_WEBHOOK_SECRET
# (live) are in Infisical.
#
# GBP live prices (D-153 fix, 2026-07-27): the original MXN live Prices
# (149/199000/19900 MXN) predated D-153's move of platform billing to GBP —
# code/config said GBP but the live Stripe Price objects were never
# recreated, so checkout was silently still charging MXN. Replaced with 3
# new GBP Prices on prod_ExampleGbpPlans (£7.99/mo, £79.90/yr, £5.99/mo
# founding); the old MXN prices are deactivated (not deleted — Stripe
# retains them for historical invoice/reporting references). Matches
# packages/shared's PLAN_PRICE_MINOR_UNITS_BY_CURRENCY.GBP and preview's
# equivalent test-mode prices in preview.runtime.env.
STRIPE_PRICE_MONTHLY=__LOCAL__
STRIPE_PRICE_ANNUAL=__LOCAL__
STRIPE_PRICE_FOUNDING=__LOCAL__
# The Customer Portal configuration this repo declares
# (apps/web/src/lib/stripe/portal-configuration.ts), applied by
# `pnpm --filter spiralclass-web stripe:portal:sync --apply`. A non-secret id,
# so it lives here beside the Price ids rather than in Infisical.
#
# Created live on 2026-09-01. The account had NO portal configuration at all
# before that, so Stripe marked this one `is_default` and it applies to every
# session already — pinning it here is what makes that explicit rather than
# incidental, and what stops a future Dashboard-created default from quietly
# taking over. Re-running the sync updates this same object in place; it is
# found by its `spiralclass_managed` metadata marker, not by this id.
STRIPE_BILLING_PORTAL_CONFIG_ID=__LOCAL__

# LiveKit (in-class video call). Non-secret halves — the websocket URL is
# already handed to the client in the join grant, and API_KEY is only the
# identifier half. LIVEKIT_API_SECRET (signs tokens) stays in Infisical.
#
# D-16 (2026-07-21): cut production over to the same self-hosted deployment
# preview already uses (docs/deployment/ORACLE_LIVEKIT_PRODUCTION.md), replacing
# LiveKit Cloud. Same RTC_PROVIDER="livekit" — LiveKitProvider talks to any
# LiveKit-API-compatible server, self-hosted or Cloud
# (docs/features/live-calls-video.md) — so this is
# purely a config change, zero app code. The box is a deliberate, documented
# risk acceptance — see D-16 and ORACLE_LIVEKIT_PRODUCTION.md for the capacity
# ceiling and the graduation trigger to a dedicated box.
#
# ⚠️ THE PAIR IS PRODUCTION'S ALONE. The box's livekit.yaml is rendered from
# Infisical's PRODUCTION environment by scripts/oracle-render-livekit.sh, so
# this key and production's LIVEKIT_API_SECRET match the box by construction.
# Preview holds no LiveKit pair at all (since 2026-09-16, D-16), so no other
# environment's value is ever copied here, or this one there. Rotating the pair
# means production's copies and a redeploy of the box:
# infra/oracle-box/CUTOVER.md step 9.
#
# Rollback: revert these two lines to the LiveKit Cloud values below (kept as
# a comment) + the matching Infisical secret, redeploy.
#   (LiveKit Cloud, pre-D-94: LIVEKIT_URL=wss://<project>.livekit.cloud, LIVEKIT_API_KEY=<redacted>)
# D-138: moved 2026-08-29 once the Oracle box actually held a certificate for
# livekit.spiralclass.com (Let's Encrypt via tls-alpn-01, expires 2026-11-27).
# Caddy still serves BOTH hostnames, so the old one keeps working for anything
# that has not picked this up.
#
# On 2026-09-19 production went to LiveKit Cloud when the Oracle box was
# lost; on 2026-09-24 it came back to livekit.spiralclass.com (D-16), now a
# free Compute Engine e2-micro rather than the Oracle box: livekit-server and
# Caddy only, NO egress (infra/gcp-livekit/). The comments above about
# rendering livekit.yaml from Infisical describe the Oracle box; the GCE box
# takes its pair from instance metadata instead — infra/gcp-livekit/README.md.
# The pair in Infisical must be the box's own (D-16's third condition).
#
# Rollback to LiveKit Cloud: restore the line below together with the Cloud
# project's pair in Infisical, and redeploy.
#   LIVEKIT_URL=wss://spiralclass-qzx0z7t7.livekit.cloud
LIVEKIT_URL=wss://livekit.spiralclass.com
LIVEKIT_API_KEY=__LOCAL__
# Selects the active VideoProvider (docs/features/live-calls-video.md).
# Explicit so a future flip to a second provider is a
# one-line diff here. lib/video/providers/index.ts
RTC_PROVIDER=livekit

# ── The gated flags were turned on here 2026-07-21; recording and
# transcription went back off 2026-08-08 ahead of the first promotion, on
# again 2026-08-26, and OFF again 2026-09-24, for capacity rather than
# policy: both needed egress, and the e2-micro production video now runs on
# cannot carry it (measured — D-16). The control that
# decides whose voice is captured is unchanged: the recorded per-pairing
# consent (D-22), guardian-only for a minor.
#
# D-185 (2026-09-28) turns TRANSCRIPTION back on without egress: the class
# transcript is now the caption text the participants' browsers already
# recognise (D-185), kept — text only, never audio — for a pairing with
# recorded insights consent, and read by Phase C exactly as before.
#
#   LESSON_INSIGHTS_TRANSCRIPTION_ENABLED — ON. While the teacher has captions
#     on, each recognised line is POSTed to /api/captions/transcript and
#     appended to the booking's LessonTranscript
#     (lib/transcription/browser-transcript.ts); the transcript is finalised
#     on room_finished (or by the Inngest fallback after the scheduled end)
#     and `lesson.transcript.ready` fires. Needs no vendor key of its own; the
#     focus areas it feeds need ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. The legacy egress capture
#     behind the same flag (call-recording.ts's maybeStartLessonAudioCapture)
#     now also requires CLASS_RECORDING_ENABLED, so this flag alone starts no
#     egress on the box.
#   CLASS_RECORDING_ENABLED — OFF (D-16): the teacher's Record control and the
#     room-composite recording (lib/video/recording.ts) need egress, which the
#     e2-micro cannot carry. It also needs LIVEKIT_EGRESS_S3_* (Tofu-owned, not
#     in this file — see preview.runtime.env's header for why grepping the repo
#     for it is misleading). Turning it back on needs a box with room for
#     egress, and means removing the recording "switched off" sentences from
#     packages/shared/src/legal/privacy-policy.ts in the same change —
#     apps/web/tests/config/ai-marketing-claims.test.ts pins both flags against
#     the policy's prose, in both directions.
LESSON_INSIGHTS_TRANSCRIPTION_ENABLED=1
# CLASS_RECORDING_ENABLED=1
#
# STILL ON — untouched by the 2026-08-08 switch-off. Captions are recognised and translated in
# the participants' browsers and published back into the room (D-185); the
# lines themselves are kept only as the class transcript above, and only with
# the pairing's insights consent (D-185), which is why captions are not part
# of the same rollback. LIVE_CAPTIONS_ENABLED additionally needs
# GOOGLE_TRANSLATE_API_KEY in production Infisical, or the caption toggle stays
# hidden despite the flag and the app logs one boot warning naming the missing
# key.
# lib/captions/config.ts
LIVE_CAPTIONS_ENABLED=1
